/-!
# Left adjoints to the truncation functors: skeleta

The left adjoints to the truncation functors of simplicial objects (the skeleton functors), their
description as colimits over truncated coslice categories, and the degeneracy of the simplices
above the truncation level.
-/

/-!
## Left adjoints to the skeleton functors

Let `C` be a category and `m : ℕ`. The skeleton functor `sk_m : Simp(C) ⥤ Simp_m(C)` restricting
a simplicial object to the full subcategory `Δ_{≤ m} ⊆ Δ` admits a left adjoint `i_{m!}` as soon
as `C` has *finite* colimits, and then

`(i_{m!}U)_n = colim_{(⦋n⦌/Δ)^{opp}_{≤ m}} U`,

the colimit of `U` over the category of morphisms `α : ⦋n⦌ ⟶ ⦋k⦌` with `k ≤ m`. Those index
categories have finitely many objects and finitely many morphisms, so no cocompleteness of `C` is
needed. In Mathlib's language `i_{m!}` is `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.Truncated.sk m`, the
left Kan extension along `(SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion m).op`, with adjunction
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.skAdj m`.

The composite `i_{n!} sk_n` is the `n`-skeleton, and it identifies with the part of its argument
generated by the simplices of degree `≤ n`. For a simplicial *set* `X` the counit
`i_{n!} sk_n X ⟶ X` is a monomorphism onto the subcomplex generated by the simplices of dimension
`≤ n`; for a simplicial object of an *abelian* category the counit is degreewise monic and its
subobject of `U_m` is the sum `Σ_{φ : ⦋m⦌ → ⦋i⦌, i ≤ n} Im(U(φ))`, the least subobject through
which all the operators coming from the degrees `≤ n` factor. Above degree `m` the normalized
Moore subobjects of `i_{m!}U` vanish.

For simplicial sets the skeleta give the cell structure of an inclusion. Adjoining to a
subcomplex `U ⊆ V` a single simplex `x` whose boundary already lies in `U`, and which is the only
thing `V` has that `U` does not, presents `V` as a pushout of the boundary inclusion
`∂Δ[n] ⟶ Δ[n]` along `U`; and when only finitely many nondegenerate simplices of `V` lie outside
`U`, the inclusion `U ⊆ V` factors as a finite sequence of such one-cell attachments. Finally,
skeleta of standard simplices compute coskeleta: `(cosk_n sk_n V)_m` represents
`X ↦ Mor(X × i_{n!} sk_n Δ[m], V)`, so for `m = n + 1`, where `i_{n!} sk_n Δ[n + 1] = ∂Δ[n + 1]`,
a morphism into it is a matching family.

### Main results

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.Truncated.hasPointwiseLeftKanExtension`: an `m`-truncated
  simplicial object of a category with finite colimits has a pointwise left Kan extension along
  `(SimplexCategory.Truncated.inclusion m).op`; equivalently `i_{m!}` exists and is given by the
  colimit formula above.
* `SSet.exists_iso_skeleton_hom_ι_eq_skAdj_counit`: for a simplicial set, the counit
  `i_{n!} sk_n X ⟶ X` factors as an isomorphism onto the subcomplex `X.skeleton (n + 1)` followed
  by the inclusion of that subcomplex.
* `SSet.Subcomplex.isPushout_boundary_ι`: adjoining one nondegenerate simplex to a subcomplex is
  a pushout of the boundary inclusion `∂Δ[n] ⟶ Δ[n]`.
* `SSet.Subcomplex.exists_monotone_sup_ofSimplex_eq_top`: an inclusion of simplicial sets with
  finitely many nondegenerate simplices outside the source is a finite sequence of one-cell
  attachments.
* `AlgebraicTopology.NormalizedMooreComplex.objX_sk_obj_eq_bot`: for `n > m`, the degree `n`
  normalized Moore subobject of `i_{m!}U` is `⊥`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.isLeast_subobject_mk_skAdj_counit_app`: for a simplicial object
  of an abelian category, the counit `i_{n!} sk_n U ⟶ U` is degreewise monic and its subobject of
  `U_m` is the least one through which every `U(φ) : U_i ⟶ U_m` with `i ≤ n` factors.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialObject.nonempty_representableBy_hom_sk_stdSimplex`: the object of
  `m`-simplices of `cosk_n sk_n V` represents `X ↦ Mor(X × i_{n!} sk_n Δ[m], V)`.

### References

* [Stacks, Tag 018L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/018L)
